+# Cancellation
+
+For whoever changes pantry order cancellation or answers a member who cannot cancel. Members may cancel before
+packing starts, two hours before their pickup slot. Late cancellations had left packed bags on the shelf for three
+Saturdays in a row; a banner asking members to cancel earlier had been in place since summer, but 25 bags of fresh
+food were thrown away in October.
+
+## Cutoff
+
+Cancellation closes when packing starts. Volunteers reported that cancellations before the packing shift cost
+nothing, while each cancellation after it starts costs a packed bag.
+
+The cutoff check lives in [`can_cancel`](../../larder/cancellation.py). At exactly two hours before the pickup slot,
+cancellation is already closed: for a 17:00 pickup, a member can cancel before 15:00, but not at 15:00 or later.
+
+## After the cutoff
+
+A member who cannot attend after the cutoff calls the pantry, and volunteers decide how to handle the pantry order.
+The [issue discussion](../../notes/issue-31.md) requires the refusal message to include the pantry phone number.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The repository contains the cutoff check, but no refusal-message implementation or pantry phone number, so it does
+not establish whether the message includes the number. When handling a late cancellation, use the pantry's current
+contact details to reach the volunteers.
